{
 "_doc": "Look of the blast effects (native/src/render/effects). Style values, matched by eye to the photos of the reference game (ports/demolition/photos-4.0.md), not physics: the physics of the blow (what it destroys, how far) is data/catalog/blast.json. Puff kinds are those of render/shaders/puffs.gdshader. A burst is count puffs of a kind over spread (metres plus a share of the fireball radius) at a height, each of size_m plus a share of the radius and a life in seconds; kind -1 is the soil's dust (earth dust over earth, concrete dust elsewhere). The fireball radius is base_m + per_force_m x force (the reference game's own law, actionsWiring.ts: 2.5 + 1.1 x strength metres, 8 m at force 5 and 52 m at 45; measured against its photographs: the physical W^(1/3) law gave 35 m at force 45 and a fireball a third too small). The shock ring and the damage reach come from the blast model. tints: the colours (sRGB) of what a blow throws and leaves, by what it is: shrapnel of the ground, poles and posts, wrecks, leaves, the ground a crater heaves, read by every effect that draws them (picked by eye, no measured value). The ring races out to reach_r fireball radii (a modelling choice: the front of the blast seen past the fireball).",
